' 34 The process harnesses of P9: N2 and the replay of spaces across blocks.
' Each child is a fresh process of the same test binary, so a result that
' depends on the memory of one process differs between the runs.
'
' Source of the harness figure of ../verification.md (section 34.9). The
' figure restates the suite rholang/tests/reified_cross_process.rs, its
' process support rholang/tests/support/process.rs and the native
' certification of rholang/tests/support/native.rs (P9 design v2, section 6,
' amendments A14 and A16). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order, from the top to the bottom:
'   1. N2: the children n2-a and n2-b each play the deploy set of N2 over an
'      in-memory store, and the parent plays it twice. The four runs give
'      the same record for each deploy.
'   2. The replay across blocks: the child propose plays three blocks over
'      one LMDB store. The child validate opens the store in another process
'      and certifies each deploy once from its pre-state, as a validator
'      does. The parent plays the blocks again and compares the records.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 34-p9-process-harnesses.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 34-p9-process-harnesses
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $rrs_relation
  LifeLineBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ParticipantBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ActorBorderColor $rrs_relation
  GroupBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
}
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam CollectionsBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The process harnesses of P9: N2 and the replay across blocks
autonumber

participant "Parent process\ntest function" as PARENT $rrs_host
participant "Children\nn2-a and n2-b" as N2 $rrs_host
participant "Child propose" as PROPOSE $rrs_host
database "LMDB store\nrun directory" as STORE $rrs_storage
collections "Deploy records\nrun directory" as RECORDS $rrs_storage
participant "Child validate" as VALIDATE $rrs_host

== N2: one deploy set in four runs ==
PARENT -[$rrs_flow]> N2 : start the test binary again (current_exe)\nwith a role variable, one child at a time
N2 -[$rrs_flow]> N2 : native play of the 62 deploys\nover an in-memory store, at the v6 limits
N2 -[$rrs_effect]> RECORDS : one record for each deploy
PARENT -[$rrs_flow]> PARENT : play the same 62 deploys twice\nin the parent process
PARENT -[$rrs_relation]> RECORDS : read the records of n2-a and n2-b
PARENT -[$rrs_relation]-> PARENT : the four runs give equal records

== The replay across blocks ==
PARENT -[$rrs_flow]> PROPOSE : start the child propose
PROPOSE -[$rrs_flow]> STORE : open the store
PROPOSE -[$rrs_flow]> PROPOSE : native play of blocks 1, 2 and 3:\n30, 28 and 28 deploys at the v6 limits
PROPOSE -[$rrs_effect]> STORE : the post-state of each deploy
PROPOSE -[$rrs_effect]> RECORDS : one record for each deploy
PARENT -[$rrs_flow]> VALIDATE : start the child validate
VALIDATE -[$rrs_relation]> RECORDS : read the records of propose
VALIDATE -[$rrs_flow]> STORE : open the store at the pre-state\nroot of the first deploy
loop each of the 86 deploys, once
  VALIDATE -[$rrs_relation]> VALIDATE : decode the evidence, check the journal,\nbind the trace to the event log
  VALIDATE -[$rrs_flow]> STORE : native replay from the pre-state,\ncompleteness check, export
  VALIDATE -[$rrs_relation]-> VALIDATE : the post-state root of play\nand the phlo of play
end
PARENT -[$rrs_relation]> RECORDS : read the records of propose
PARENT -[$rrs_relation]-> PARENT : each deploy starts at the\npost-state root of the deploy before it
PARENT -[$rrs_flow]> PARENT : play the three blocks again over\nan in-memory store, in the parent process
PARENT -[$rrs_relation]-> PARENT : equal records, and the deliveries\nof each family and of the agent

note over PARENT, VALIDATE
A record holds the pre-state and post-state roots, the outputs, the event log,
the evidence bytes, the phlo and the host work of play. A child prints no test
output to the parent: the parent keeps the standard output of each child.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_host>       | process of the test binary |
|<$rrs_storage>    | stored state and the record files |
**Arrows**
|<$rrs_flow>       | start, play or replay |
|<$rrs_effect>     | write to a store or to a record file |
|<$rrs_relation>   | read, check or result |
endlegend
@enduml
